To convert an InputStream to a String in Java, you can use the `read()` method, which reads the InputStream into a byte array. Then, you can use the `String` constructor to convert the byte array into a String.

Here is a simple example:

```java
import java.io.InputStream;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        InputStream inputStream = System.in;
        String str = convertStreamToString(inputStream);
        System.out.println(str);
    }

    public static String convertStreamToString(InputStream is) {
        byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];
        int len;
        while ((len = is.read(buffer)) != -1) {
            String str = new String(buffer, 0, len);
            return str;
        }
        return "";
    }
}
```

